WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.835
-Our first guest tonight
is a United States Senator

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.203
from Massachusetts.

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:07.240
Please welcome back to the show
Senator Elizabeth Warren!

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.175
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:15.982 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:22.822 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.123
Welcome to the show, Senator.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:27.927
Well, it has been -- it has been
a week of historic news.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.495
Not all good, most bad.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:32.632
But let's start
with a silver lining.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.966
Judge Ketanji Brown-Jackson

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.869
becomes the first Black woman
on the Supreme Court.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.270
-Yes.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.438
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:40.974
You know her other first?

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:44.811
She is the first public defender

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.647
to sit on the United States
Supreme Court.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.115
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.383
Think about --

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.885
Just for one second,
think about what that means.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:56.755
This is a woman who has made
public service her life

00:00:56.755 --> 00:01:00.493
and who is so committed
to the principles of justice

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:04.163
that she made her work
about speaking up for people

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.931
who couldn't afford
to have lawyers,

00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:07.634
who weren't
going to have a voice

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:12.171
except for someone like her
who stepped in

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.207
and said, "That's my job
and I'm going to be

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.675
part of making this
justice system work."

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.343
She's going to be fabulous
on the Supreme Court.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.778
-That's a really interesting
point

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.546
because I think we often talk
about the hegemony of, like,

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:22.882
how the backgrounds and
sort of the racial backgrounds

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.418
or, you know,
the gender backgrounds --

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.720
But really that's such
a interesting point,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.223
because everybody comes from it
from the same side of the law.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.291
And, of course,
the law is multifaceted.

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.826
So that'll be great to have
that new perspective.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.828
-That's right.
We have had a lot of people

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.397
who came from the side
of all those corporations

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.934
who desperately needed help.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.370
-And now
it's really terrific to have --

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.739
It's kind of amazing
it took us this long, right,

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.608
that we have
our first public defender.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.109
She's going to be terrific.

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:53.078
-Unfortunately, it seems like
a lot of her role will be

00:01:53.078 --> 00:01:57.383
to be one of 3 people
on the side of 6-3 decisions.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.153
You know, we had another one
today about emissions.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:03.689
Basically, the court ruled
that the EPA is very limited

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:06.259
in the sort of emissions

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.895
they can regulate
from different plants.

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:11.597
What are
the grander implications

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.032
of a decision like this?

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.201
-So, look,
this is a Supreme Court

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:18.804
that is basically
out of control.

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:20.640
And they have decided

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.610
that they don't like
the way that we have,

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:29.448
for decades now, tried
to deal with climate change.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.884
This has been a very
pro-corporate court,

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:33.219
and this is actually

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.322
not the first decision
in that direction.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:40.559
They've been anti-union.
They've been anti-consumer.

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:44.597
They've empowered corporations
more than ever before,

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.433
giving them
religious liberty rights,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:51.270
letting them contribute
money, money, money

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.340
to influence
the political process.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.010
And I see this as just --
this is one more decision

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:02.281
heaped on losing
Roe versus Wade,

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:06.886
heaped on a gun decision
that is going to make life

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.555
more dangerous
for all of our children,

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:13.792
for all of our neighbors,
for all of our loved ones.

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:17.530
It really is a time
when the American people

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.200
are losing confidence
in the Supreme Court,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.304
and for good reason.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.238
A court
that is not grounded in law,

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:29.576
not grounded in, uh...

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:34.413
in the principles
on which we have tried

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:36.849
to build a country
going forward,

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.652
but instead a court
that says, nope, they're just

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:43.689
going to substitute
their own personal views

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.691
and make the rest of America
bend to it.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.326
-So this is a time
where I feel like --

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.529
You must be hearing this a lot
from your constituents,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.963
from the people you talk to.

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:53.065
It seems like there's
two reactions you have,

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.967
which is to be sad
or to be angry.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.603
Do you feel like one
is more helpful than the other?

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.138
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:02.308
-Sad.
You got a few hours for that.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:05.978
-Okay.
-I will go as much as 24.

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:07.446
-To 2 to 24 hours.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.982
-And that's it. That's it.
2 to 24 hours.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:12.885
And after that,
cold bucket of water.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:16.755
Because now
it is time to be angry

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:20.158
and to channel that anger
into action.

00:04:20.158 --> 00:04:23.963
And the reason for that is sad
is about leaning back

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.499
and giving up,
and we can't do that.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.767
There is a path out of this.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:32.138
It is not an easy path.
It is not a guaranteed win.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.573
But I guarantee you this --

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.107
you don't get
what you don't fight for.

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:37.743
So it is powerfully important

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:41.547
to take the anger over what
the Supreme Court has done

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.982
and channel it into action.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.917
Can we do the actions?
-Let's do the actions.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.552
-Let's do it. Alright.
Let's do it.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.821
Right now on Roe,
the first one is

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.190
there are people out there
right now

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.659
who are pregnant
and who need help.

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.428
They need protection.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:59.399
And we need to pour resources
into helping them.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.434
That means each of us
volunteering money,

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:05.437
volunteering time
to support the organizations

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:07.240
that are trying to help people.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.542
The administration is stepping
in, using all of its tools.

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.313
And I commend the President
for stepping up,

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.115
for example,
on medication abortion,

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.017
making that
more widely available,

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.752
protecting people
who have to cross state lines

00:05:20.752 --> 00:05:22.354
in order to get help.

00:05:22.354 --> 00:05:24.423
We should be looking at the fact
that the federal government,

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.458
biggest employer
in the country --

00:05:26.458 --> 00:05:28.661
make sure that people
have got time off from work

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.162
and resources to travel.

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:32.164
So we need to do things
to protect people

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:33.899
who are pregnant now

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.936
and who get pregnant next month
and the next month,

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.738
because this is the
urgent problem in front of us.

00:05:39.738 --> 00:05:41.673
But second thing we need to do

00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:45.178
is we got to focus like a laser

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.980
on the election in November.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:52.084
Understand --
this small minority

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:55.687
that wanted to overturn Roe
has been disciplined.

00:05:55.687 --> 00:06:00.126
They have worked at this
for nearly five decades.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:03.796
They lost and they got back up
and they stayed in the fight.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.899
And they helped
all of those senators

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:10.402
who help shepherd through
these justices

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:12.671
who swore
until the world looked level

00:06:12.671 --> 00:06:14.506
that Roe was settled law

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:16.609
and that we don't disturb
settled law.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:20.145
And as soon as they got
the votes, they went ahead

00:06:20.145 --> 00:06:22.448
and did not just
to chip away at Roe --

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.383
just blew the whole thing up.

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:26.952
We need to be just as committed,

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:32.691
just as focused
on this election in November.

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:34.193
Two senators.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:38.230
If we pick up
two Democratic senators

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.298
who will help us
get rid of the filibuster,

00:06:40.298 --> 00:06:43.502
which the President has now said
he's on board for that,

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:46.272
and who will give us
Roe versus Wade --

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.940
Two senators.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.644
And, yes, John Fetterman, I am
looking at you in Pennsylvania.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:55.681
Yes, Mandela Barnes,
I'm looking at you in Wisconsin.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:59.218
We get those two senators in,
we hang on to the House,

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.320
and Roe versus Wade

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.590
will be the law
all across America.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.593
That's what we can get done.
That's a fight worth having.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.562
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-I think it's important --

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:12.531
And I appreciate the optimism.

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:14.667
What do you say to people
who feel as though

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.969
maybe Democratic leadership

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.937
did get caught
a little flat-footed from --

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:20.939
I mean, it did feel like this
was coming for 50 years.

00:07:20.939 --> 00:07:22.808
Now, maybe nobody thought
it was going to happen.

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:24.643
But we've certainly known
for the last few months,

00:07:24.643 --> 00:07:26.912
based on the leaked draft,
this was coming.

00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:29.748
And it did seem like
it took the White House

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:32.951
maybe six days to come out
sort of with their plan.

00:07:32.951 --> 00:07:34.553
Why wasn't there
a plan in place,

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:36.822
or was there and it was
just slow to come out?

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:39.392
-Look, I think what matters

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:44.163
is that we are using
every tool in the toolbox

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:48.033
and doing everything we can
to protect people

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:51.336
who are pregnant right now
and need help.

00:07:51.336 --> 00:07:54.106
But understand this --

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:58.210
we have every single Republican

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:00.112
in the United States Senate
and the House

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:02.748
has voted against
Roe versus Wade.

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:05.918
We actually had this --
Nobody quite remembers this.

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:09.355
Just a few weeks ago,
we actually voted this

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:11.056
in the Senate,

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:16.495
and every Republican said nope
on Roe versus Wade.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:18.530
You know what?
We got elections coming up.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:22.935
We need to hold every Republican
accountable for those votes.

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:25.504
-I have a lot more to ask you.
We will be right back with more

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:27.540
from Senator Elizabeth Warren.

